{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Exploration: Alpha**\n\nFound 3 symbols across 3 files.\n\n**Blast radius — what depends on these (update/verify before editing)**\n\n- `Alpha` (pkga/pkga.go:15) — 1 caller in `pkga/pkga.go`; ⚠️ no covering tests found\n- `main` (main.go:16) — 0 callers in `main.go`\n- `Helper` (pkgb/pkgb.go:9) — 2 callers in `pkgb/pkgb.go`; ⚠️ no covering tests found\n\n**Source Code**\n\n\u003e The code below is the **verbatim, current on-disk source** of these files — re-read from disk on this call and line-numbered, byte-for-byte identical to what the Read tool returns. It is NOT a summary, outline, or stale cache. Treat each block as a Read you have already performed: do not Read a file shown here.\n\n**`pkga/pkga.go`** — Alpha(function)\n\n```go\n1\t// FROZEN: this tree is checked in solely for the wire oracle\n2\t// (testdata/wireoracle/fixture) and must not be edited once transcripts\n3\t// under testdata/wireoracle/transcripts/ are frozen (D-08).\n4\t\n5\t// Package pkga exports two functions where one calls the other, plus a\n6\t// cross-package call into pkgb — the shape the wire oracle's\n7\t// handshake-explore scenario queries against.\n8\tpackage pkga\n9\t\n10\timport \"wireoraclefixture/pkgb\"\n11\t\n12\t// Alpha is an exported function that calls Beta (intra-package) and\n13\t// pkgb.Helper (cross-package). This is the symbol name the\n14\t// handshake-explore scenario's codegraph_explore query argument names.\n15\tfunc Alpha() string {\n16\t\treturn Beta() + pkgb.Helper()\n17\t}\n18\t\n19\t// Beta is an exported function called by Alpha.\n20\tfunc Beta() string {\n21\t\treturn \"beta\"\n22\t}\n```\n\n**`main.go`** — main(function)\n\n```go\n1\t// FROZEN: this tree is checked in solely for the wire oracle\n2\t// (testdata/wireoracle/fixture) and must not be edited once transcripts\n3\t// under testdata/wireoracle/transcripts/ are frozen (D-08).\n4\t\n5\t// Command wireoraclefixture is the wire oracle's dedicated, purpose-built\n6\t// discovery fixture — calling into both packages below.\n7\tpackage main\n8\t\n9\timport (\n10\t\t\"fmt\"\n11\t\n12\t\t\"wireoraclefixture/pkga\"\n13\t\t\"wireoraclefixture/pkgb\"\n14\t)\n15\t\n16\tfunc main() {\n17\t\tfmt.Println(pkga.Alpha())\n18\t\tfmt.Println(pkgb.Helper())\n19\t}\n```\n\n**`pkgb/pkgb.go`** — Helper(function)\n\n```go\n1\t// FROZEN: this tree is checked in solely for the wire oracle\n2\t// (testdata/wireoracle/fixture) and must not be edited once transcripts\n3\t// under testdata/wireoracle/transcripts/ are frozen (D-08).\n4\t\n5\t// Package pkgb exports one function pkga.Alpha calls (cross-package call).\n6\tpackage pkgb\n7\t\n8\t// Helper is an exported function that pkga.Alpha calls.\n9\tfunc Helper() string {\n10\t\treturn \"helper\"\n11\t}\n```\n\n"}]}}
